findings.body:
**Compare the receipt identity with `reviewDigest(identity_inputs)` in the local harvest validator.**

`validateLocalReviewReceipt` checks only the identity format and the schema shape. It does not compare `identity` with the digest of `identity_inputs`, so a receipt with a mismatched pair passes validation and is written. The result consumer rejects the same pair. Add the comparison to the validator so the local harvest enforces the same rule.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
-import { IdentitySchema, ReceiptSchema } from '../../ops/review/internal/reviewOperation.js';
+import { IdentitySchema, ReceiptSchema, reviewDigest } from '../../ops/review/internal/reviewOperation.js';
@@
 export function validateLocalReviewReceipt(value: JsonObject): void {
   version(value);
   const identity = value.get('identity_inputs');
   if (!(identity instanceof JsonObject)) throw new Error('invalid identity');
   validateLocalReviewIdentity(identity);
-  ReceiptSchema.parse(toPlainJson(value));
+  const receipt = ReceiptSchema.parse(toPlainJson(value));
+  if (reviewDigest(receipt.identity_inputs) !== receipt.identity)
+    throw new Error('receipt identity mismatch');
 }
```

</details>
